<HelloFraandsPage title="Payment & wallet terms" summary="Wallet ka balance sirf platform par baat karne ke liye hai." review={true} related={[{"href":"/refunds","label":"Refunds"},{"href":"/terms","label":"Terms of use"},{"href":"/grievance","label":"Grievance redressal"}]}>
<h2>Planned wallet, not an active payment offer</h2>
<p>The website is a preview. Top-ups, paid calls, settlement, and wallet safeguards described here are planned; do not treat example balances or rates as a payment confirmation. Final payment and wallet terms must be approved and shown before accepting money.</p>
<h2>Rate and minimum balance</h2>
<p>The launch design uses a host-set per-minute rate with a general-lane floor of ₹20/minute; the women-only lane may have a separate floor. The chosen host's actual rate must be shown before a call. A caller needs at least two minutes of balance at that rate to start.</p>
<h2>When charges start</h2>
<p>Billing starts only when host and caller are connected, not while a phone rings or the host decides. Launch billing is per started minute: for example, 61 connected seconds at ₹20/minute costs ₹40. Declines, timeouts before connection, and failed bridges cost nothing.</p>
<p>The planned maximum duration is the number of whole minutes the available balance buys, capped at 60 minutes per call. A warning is planned 60 seconds before this limit, followed by automatic disconnection at the limit. These controls require backend implementation and testing.</p>
<h2>Settlement and host earnings</h2>
<p>Each call is intended to settle once against its connection and end records. The planned platform share per minute is ₹2 plus 40% of the amount above ₹2. At ₹20/minute, this is ₹9.20 for the platform and ₹10.80 for the host. The specification includes 18% GST within the platform share; final tax treatment and receipts require review before launch.</p>
<p>Host earnings and caller prepaid balances are separate records. Top-up methods, payout eligibility and timing, expiry, promotional credits, and unused-balance withdrawal or refund conditions are not finalised by this preview.</p>
<h2>Ended calls, restrictions, and disputes</h2>
<p>A host block or moderation cut bills connected time under the same started-minute rule; it does not itself forfeit unused balance. The specification proposes forfeiture only after a ban based on three confirmed strikes. That proposal remains subject to legal review and a complaint process, not an automatic right asserted by this preview.</p>
<p>See <a href="/refunds">refunds and billing disputes</a> for missing credits or incorrect charges, and <a href="/grievance">grievance redressal</a> for review of account restrictions.</p>
